    "finding": "The isolated push guard rejects a push with NV_ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED when its tracker contains pending work owned by another GPU. The resident-copy path submits two mapping-invalidation batches, then populates/copies; service then proceeds into revoke and map phases. These source paths have no tracker-wait/retry boundary between those phases. Therefore an owner transition can be refused while foreign-GPU work is still pending. This is conditional on runtime tracker completion and does not prove that every direct migration fails.",
